Hello wonderful world of unmarked,

I am running bird models in gdistsamp and am also encountering this issue when trying to run parboot.  I have a top model that looks great (standardized covs, simulations look good), but at some point in the parboot, a sim doesn't work, gets an "error in optim", then the parboot stops.  Ideally, I'm trying to run 100 sims, but I've managed to lower the number of sims for a couple of species (50 or 75 sims) and eventually it will run all the way through so I get my GoF stat.  I would, however, like to have at least 100 sims for each species so I'm looking for help in implementing this "trycatch" code.  Richard Schuster (or anyone!), would you be willing to walk me through the "try" code??

Many thanks in advance for any help, and I'm happy to post/send code as needed.
Melissa Roach

