100% 1.6e+15

I would appreciate any insights in to what may be causing this. Perhaps I am missing something obvious. Could it be an artefact of a zero-inflated dataset or small sample size? Attached is some shortened reproducible code and the datset.

Moving forward would it be best to select an alternative mixture? In testing both the Poisson and ZIP we found none of them to have this issue, whereas for NB it occurs in many of the models. K was set to 100 for the final models, and was tested at higher intervals (200, 500, 1000, 5000) with no change in abundance estimates.

