Hi John and Marc,

Thanks for your replies and comments. Just to clarify the n=162 is sites (23) x replicates (8) with missing surveys removed (i.e. some sites were padded with NAs where less replicates occurred). As I'm using AICc rather than AIC to assess goodness of fit due to small sample size I tested the models with n set to both just to see if there was much difference in the model selection.

I has previously read the references you suggest, and I thank you for drawing me back to them as they do make some very interesting points which I had not considered when addressing the underdispersion issue. Based on this and your comments I will move forward with the Poisson mixture and see if that gives me ecologically sensible estimates.

I greatly appreciate your time and will also pass your comments on to my friendly neighbourhood statistical ecologist who was interested in the outcome of this.

Many thanks,

Rob

